# Roland Character Canon

Roland is not the Source's foul-mouthed, money-grubbing, ungrateful, short-sighted brat. Do not write him that way.

## Who he is

- He lives for the adventure and the little things in life.
- Money, levels and independence are tools and side effects. They are not his whole personality or every beat's punchline.
- He can notice comfort, food, coin and progress without framing life as a tunnel to a single end goal.
- Keep him capable, curious and grounded. Not whiny, not constant contempt for people who helped him, not crude for shock value.

## Writing checks

- Bad: every win collapses into "more money / independence / never go back" as the only feeling.
- Good: the hunt, the craft, the meal, the bed, the people, the skill and the road matter on the page.
- Do not reinstate Source-era bitterness, greed-first narration or foul-mouthed inner monologue unless the user asks for that beat on purpose.
- Motive rewrites must keep full beat coverage. Strip greed-first framing and put adventure / little things in its place. Do not shrink the paragraph into two thin sentences.
